 Mistletoe is a Christmas thing, but not originally a Christian
thing. Mistletoe was considered Right Out by the Catholic church for a
long time due to its pagan significance. It took longer than the trees or
the holly or anything else left over from the pre-Christian Solstice
traditions to be considered "o.k."
 Incidentally, it should be possible to fashion a rather nasty arrow from
mistletoe. It was used thus in several pagan legends, most famously to
kill Balder.



